6. Layer 4 — Neural Computation (original)

We retain the free‑energy principle and predictive coding framework:

F = \mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}[q(s)\|p(s|o)] - \ln p(o). \tag{9}

Under the Laplace approximation, gradient descent \dot{\mu} = -\partial_\mu F gives perception. For linear Gaussian models, convergence is exponential. For nonlinear systems, the thesis will develop contraction proofs based on Lipschitz constants, contributing to the formal understanding of neural dynamics.

