7. Layer 5 — Cognitive Modelling (original)

Decision: Cumulative Prospect Theory value V = \sum w(p_i)v(x_i) with v(x)=x^\alpha (gains), -\lambda(-x)^\alpha (losses), and w(p)=p^\gamma/(p^\gamma+(1-p)^\gamma)^{1/\gamma}.

Learning: Rescorla–Wagner update converges to expected reward by stochastic approximation (Kushner & Yin, 2003).

Memory: Variable‑precision Bayesian model with capacity‑limited precision allocation.

Identifiability Theorem (to be developed). Under mild regularity conditions, the joint model of genetic effects → neural parameters → behavioural parameters is locally identifiable if the mapping from neural to behavioural parameters is injective. Proof sketch. The Fisher information matrix block‑diagonal structure arises from the conditional independence of genetic and behavioural data given neural parameters; block invertibility then ensures local identifiability.

